.org/t/p/w600_and_h900_face/wXqWR7dHncNRbxoEGybEy7QTe9h.jpg","small_backdrop_path":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w342//ff2ti5DkA9UYLzyqhQfI2kZqEuh.jpg","small_poster_path":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w342//wXqWR7dHncNRbxoEGybEy7QTe9h.jpg"},{"tmdb_id":74879,"title":"Once Upon a Time in Anatolia","description":"A group of men set out in search of a dead body in the Anatolian steppes","duration":"2:43:00","genre":["Drama","Crime"],"release_date":"2011-09-23","backdrop_path":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w600_and_h900_face/213Gdu9zjGsVeWQl6p5gJrBq8n8.jpg","poster_path":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w600_and_h900_face/bN84guFndgvtWIvFC7sTD8AAJDE.jpg","small_backdrop_path":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w342//213Gdu9zjGsVeWQl6p5gJrBq8n8.jpg","small_poster_path":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w342//bN84guFndgvtWIvFC7sTD8AAJDE.jpg"},{"tmdb_id":625,"title":"The Killing Fields","description":"New York Times reporter Sydney Schanberg is on assignment covering the Cambodian Civil War, with the help of local interpreter Dith Pran and American photojournalist Al Rockoff. When the U.S. Army pulls out amid escalating violence, Schanberg makes exit arrangements for Pran and his family. Pran, however, tells Schanberg he intends to stay in Cambodia to help cover the unfolding story — a decision he may regret as the Khmer Rouge rebels move in.","duration":"2:22:00","genre":["Drama","History","War"],"release_date":"1984-11-23","backdrop_path":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w600_and_h900_face/c7OeJd34rc9bI1DXqd4ucb1wVrf.jpg","poster_path":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w600_and_h900_face/cX6Bv7natnZwQjsV9bLL8mmWjkS.jpg","small_backdrop_path":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w342//c7OeJd34rc9bI1DXqd4ucb1wVrf.jpg","small_poster_path":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w342//cX6Bv7natnZwQjsV9bLL8mmWjkS.jpg"},{"tmdb_id":347201,"title":"Boruto: Naruto the Movie","description":"The spirited Boruto Uzumaki, son of Seventh Hokage Naruto, is a skilled ninja who possesses the same brashness and passion his father once had. How